WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.200
Skill development requires practice, feedback, correction, and repetition.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.955
Whether the skill is technical troubleshooting, writing, communication, analysis,

00:00:07.955 --> 00:00:11.300
or a physical action, learners need repeated high-quality attempts.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:15.710
Sleep supports this indirectly by supporting the attention and recovery that make repeated

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:16.630
practice useful.

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:19.600
Poor recovery can turn practice into low-quality repetition.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.385
Procedural learning, at a high level, involves getting better at how to do something,

00:00:23.385 --> 00:00:24.915
not only knowing facts about it.

00:00:24.915 --> 00:00:29.300
Automaticity can develop when parts of a skill require less conscious effort over time.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.710
That can free attention for judgment and adaptation.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:35.835
But automaticity grows from practice with feedback, not from time spent near the skill.

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:39.520
Mental rehearsal can be useful in a general way when it helps someone prepare steps,

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:42.000
anticipate decisions, or review a performance.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.400
It should not replace real practice or feedback.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.540
For example, a learner might mentally walk through a troubleshooting sequence,

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:50.205
then practice on a scenario and compare the result.

00:00:50.205 --> 00:00:53.440
Sleep and recovery help make these cycles sustainable across sessions.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:56.380
Measure skill by performance, not just time spent practicing.

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:58.300
Did the learner find defects more reliably?

00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.570
Write more clearly?

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:01.285
Ask better diagnostic questions?

00:01:01.285 --> 00:01:03.345
Communicate uncertainty more effectively?

00:01:03.345 --> 00:01:06.930
Practice time matters because it creates opportunity, but sleep, recovery,

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:10.560
and feedback influence whether that opportunity becomes real improvement.
